/*
We build a frame by appending controls to a flat box tree, then measuring children
bottom-up and arranging parents top-down. Stable, nonzero control IDs connect the
new tree to the preceding frame's hit rectangles. A host supplies pointer and
keyboard input, paints the arranged tree, and schedules another frame when input
or animation changes the model.

The context holds 128 nodes, eight nested containers, and 8192 label bytes. We keep
these stores inside the context so a frame needs no heap allocation. Text spans
carry a generation: rebuilding the frame retires every earlier label. Overflow
is explicit; this package is intended for bounded views rather than an unbounded
document tree. Docking uses a separate twelve-slot tree and has no renderer.
*/

/*
The package owns layout, controls, text storage, color roles, and software drawing.
Its host owns native windows, event pumping, and repaint policy. The Windows
adapter supplies actual font measurement, text editing, and cached bitmap painting.
Gallery-specific panels live in examples/gallery; reusable controls do not know
the gallery's page numbers, demonstration labels, or packed panel state.
Hosts call UiMotion::advance once per frame with elapsed milliseconds, then keep
scheduling while context.motion.animating is true. Set motion.reduced to snap
transitions. Rebuilding the view never advances animation time.

tests/headless/main.omg exercises layout, input, themes, text lifetimes,
Unicode validation, and raster output. @Incomplete: native accessibility and
editable numeric text are not implemented by the current number field.
*/

use types;
use motion;
use palette;
use text;
use utf16;
use context;
use dock;
use widgets;
use raster;
use tester;
use frame;
use scene;
use viewport;
use list;
use text_field;
use edit;
use paint_boxes;

// We retain the context between frames so stable IDs can find earlier hit boxes.
machine example_frame_lifecycle(label_width: i32, label_height: i32)
requires label_width >= 0 && label_height > 0 {
    let mut context: UiContext = UiContext::new(64, 64);
    UiContext::setup(&mut context, 64, 64, true);
    let mut frame: UiFrame = UiFrame::begin(&mut context);
    Ui::column(&mut context, 2, 2, true, true);
    let button_interaction: Interaction = Ui::button(&mut context, 1, "Apply",
        ButtonOptions { variant: ButtonVariant::Primary, width: 48, height: 24 });
    UiContext::set_text_metrics(&mut context, 2, label_width, label_height);
    Ui::end(&mut context);
    let rebuild: bool = UiFrame::next_pass(&mut frame, &mut context);
    let mut pixels: [i32; 4096];
    Raster::render(&context, &mut pixels);
    // The next begin_frame retires text and rebuilds nodes; no resource release is needed.
    UiContext::begin_frame(&mut context);
    UiContext::end_frame(&mut context);
}
